le ascribes to Muhammad Rumfa (1463-99) a number of innovations of varying importance, among them the extension of the city walls and the building of new gates; the appointment of eunuchs to state offices; the establishment of Kurmi market, the main market in Kano; and the setting up of a council of nine leading office-holders (tara-ta-Kano — \'the Nine of Kano\') as a kind of ministry.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 926, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 829})
